# Files bundled into the app must be byte-identical on every machine.
#
# With core.autocrlf=true, a Windows checkout turns text files into CRLF while
# a macOS/Linux CI machine keeps LF, so the same commit bundles different
# bytes depending on who built it. Code push (Shorebird, docs/SHOREBIRD.md)
# compares a patch with its release byte for byte and cannot patch assets:
# a patch built on Windows for a CI release would see every JSON and
# translation file as "changed" and be refused. Binary files (images, fonts)
# are detected by text=auto and left untouched.
assets/** text=auto eol=lf
shorebird.yaml text eol=lf
